card.statement:
Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a covariant admissible set of relations.

- [(i)] The
the formulas <<ref:action h>>-<<ref:action f>> define a $\gl(m|n)$-module structure on $V_{\mathcal C}([l^0])$ for any $\mathcal{C}$-covariant tableau
$[l^0]$.

- [(ii)]
The action of $B(t)$ on any basis tableau $[l]$ of $V_{\mathcal C}([l^0])$ is given by

\begin{equation}
B_k(t)[l]=
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&(1+tl_{k1})\cdots(1+tl_{kk})[l],      &\text{if } 1\leq k\leq m,\\
&\frac{(1+tl_{k1})\cdots(1+tl_{km})}
{(1+tl_{k,m+1})\cdots(1+tl_{k,k})} [l],    &\text{if } m+1\leq k\leq m+n.\\
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation}

- [(iii)] The module
$V_{\mathcal C}([l^0])$ is irreducible if and only if
$\mathcal C$ is the
maximal set of relations satisfied by $[l^0]$.
